= Crisis? What Crisis?

Callaghan flies back, suntanned, from a summit in Guadeloupe. At Heathrow, a reporter asks about the mounting chaos. He replies that he doesn't think other people in the world would share the view that there is "mounting chaos".

The next morning's Sun headline reads: **"Crisis? What Crisis?"** He never said those words, but nobody will remember that.
